content.text:
Now main.js. Let's draft carefully.

Potential import of `OutputPass`: exists in three/addons/postprocessing/OutputPass.js. Good.

Need to create the particle mesh after scene. `this.particles` etc.

Let's write.

Pseudo:

```js
import fonts...
import './style.css';
import * as THREE from 'three';
...

const SAVE_KEY='cubehaven.save.v1';
const SAVE_VERSION=1;

function smoothstep(...)
function clamp(...)
function randomSeed()...
function readSaveRaw()...

class Game {
 constructor() {
   this.settings=new Settings();
   this.atlas=getAtlas();
   this.audio=new AudioManager(this.settings);
   this.state='loading';
   this.overlayReturn='menu';
   this.world=null; this.worldSeed=null; this.player=null;
   this.worldTime=0.34; this.day=1;
   this.keys=new Set();
   this.touch={axisX:0,axisY:0,jump:false,sprint:false,down:false};
   this.isTouch=false; this.pointerLocked=false; this.dragging=false; ...
   this.selectedBlockId=DEFAULT_HOTBAR[0];
   this.swing=0; this.time=0; this.saveTimer=0; this.hudTimer=0;
   this.frames=0; this.fpsTime=0; this.fps=60;
   this.menuAngle=0.6;
   this.temps...
   this.sprintToggle=false;
   this.transitioning=false;
   this._target=null;
   this.initRenderer();
   this.initScene();
   this.initSky();
   this.initClouds();
   this.initStars();
   this.initParticles();
   this.initHeld();
   this.initHighlight();
   this.initEvents();
   this.ui = new UI(this);
   this.applySettings(true);
   this.init();
 }
```

Need UI created before initEvents? Events reference ui. We can create UI before initEvents. But UI constructor calls game.audio.ui? No. It calls game.onSlotSelected -> updateHeldItem -> heldGroup exists. Good.
Order:
- renderer/scene/sky/clouds/stars/particles/held/highlight
- ui = new UI(this)
- initEvents()
- applySettings(true)
- init()

But UI's bindGlobal adds pointerdown audio ensure to buttons. Fine.

`initRenderer`:
```
this.canvas=document.getElementById('game');
this.renderer=new THREE.WebGLRenderer({canvas,antialias:true, powerPreference:'high-performance', alpha:false});
this.renderer.outputColorSpace=THREE.SRGBColorSpace;
this.renderer.toneMapping=THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;
this.renderer.toneMappingExposure=1;
this.renderer.shadowMap.enabled=true;
this.renderer.shadowMap.type=THREE.PCFSoftShadowMap;
this.renderer.setClearColor(0x87c9ef,1);
this.camera=new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(70, innerWidth/innerHeight, 0.08, 700);
this.scene=new THREE.Scene();
this.scene.add(this.camera);
this.scene.fog=new THREE.Fog(0xbfe9ff, 30, 155);
this.resizeRenderer();
```

`initScene` lights.
- sunLight target.
- shadow map size 2048.
- `this.sunLight.shadow.camera.left=-46` etc.
- `this.sunLight.shadow.bias=-0.0006; normalBias=0.06;`
- `this.sunLight.shadow.camera.near=1; far=220`.
- `this.sunLight.castShadow=true`.
- Add.
- hemi, ambient.

Composer after scene/camera:
```
this.composer = new EffectComposer(this.renderer);
this.renderPass = new RenderPass(scene,camera);
this.bloomPass = new UnrealBloomPass(new Vector2(innerWidth, innerHeight), 0.5, 0.55, 0.85);
this.outputPass = new OutputPass();
composer.addPass(...);
composer.setSize(innerWidth,innerHeight);
```
- `this.composer.setPixelRatio(this.renderer.getPixelRatio())` after setSize? Use `composer.setPixelRatio(renderer.getPixelRatio()); composer.setSize(w,h);`. The constructor already uses pixel ratio. On resize, call both.
- Bloom strength 0.45, radius 0.5, threshold 0.82. The sky is bright; threshold 0.82 might bloom sky. Maybe threshold 1.0 and sun color >1. Use 0.9. Tone mapping is applied in OutputPass after bloom; bloom input is HDR values. Sky colors in linear maybe 0.5-1.0; sun >1. Threshold 1.0 means only sun/glowstone. Set threshold 0.95, strength 0.5, radius 0.6. Good.

Sky shader:
```
const skyGeo = new THREE.BoxGeometry(1,1,1);
const skyMat = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
 side: THREE.BackSide,
 depthWrite:false,
 depthTest:false,
 uniforms:{ uTop:{value:new Color('#3f8fd8')}, ... },
 vertexShader:`varying vec3 vDir; void main(){ vDir=position; gl_Position=projectionMatrix*modelViewMatrix*vec4(position,1.0); }`,
 fragmentShader:`...`
});
this.sky=new Mesh(...); this.sky.scale.setScalar(520); this.sky.renderOrder=-1000; this.sky.frustumCulled=false; scene.add
```
- But `depthTest:false` means sky always draws over previous frame? Renderer clears color each frame, sky draws first. Fine.
- Fragment includes tonemapping/colorspace. Does ShaderMaterial automatically add `#include <tonemapping_fragment>`? We include. Need `#include <common>`? For tonemapping, uniforms like toneMappingExposure are defined in `<tonemapping_pars_fragment>` which is injected by WebGLProgram for ShaderMaterial? For ShaderMaterial, the prefix includes tone mapping defines/uniforms only if `material.toneMapped`? I'm not 100% sure. Three's WebGLProgram prefixFragment includes `#include <tonemapping_pars_fragment>` if parameters.toneMapping !== NoToneMapping. Yes it does for all materials. Then `#include <tonemapping_fragment>` works. Similarly colorspace pars. Good.
- Set `this.skyMat = skyMat`.

Sun/moon meshes. Use BoxGeometry shared? Create `this.cubeGeo = new THREE.BoxGeometry(1,1,1)`.

Stars instanced:
```
const starGeo=new BoxGeometry(1,1,1);
const starMat=new MeshBasicMaterial({color:0xffffff, transparent:true, opacity:1, fog:false, depthWrite:false});
this.stars=new InstancedMesh(starGeo,starMat,280);
this.stars.renderOrder=-950; this.stars.frustumCulled=false;
const dummy=new Object3D();
for i: random direction with y>-0.05; pos radius 320; scale .7-1.8; dummy...; setMatrixAt; color slight; setColorAt.
this.stars.instanceMatrix.needsUpdate=true;
this.starsGroup=new Group(); this.starsGroup.add(this.stars); scene.add(starsGroup);
```
Actually InstancedMesh can be added directly to scene and position set to camera. Use `this.stars.position.copy(camera.position)` each frame. Simpler no group. Same for sun/moon individually. Set stars.position. Rotation `stars.rotation.y = time*0.005`.
- If stars is InstancedMesh and positions are on sphere radius 320, camera far 700. Good.
- `depthWrite:false`; depthTest true. Sky has no depth, so stars visible. Terrain occludes. Fine.

Clouds:
```
this.cloudMat = new MeshLambertMaterial({color:0xffffff, transparent:true, opacity:0.93, flatShading:true});
this.clouds = new InstancedMesh(new BoxGeometry(1,1,1), cloudMat, 120);
...
```
- Data.
- `this.clouds.frustumCulled=false`.
- Update matrices each frame in updateClouds.

Particles:
- `this.particleGeo = new BoxGeometry(1,1,1); this.particleMat = new MeshBasicMaterial({color:0xffffff, transparent:true, opacity:1});`
- `this.particleMesh = new InstancedMesh(geo, mat, 100); this.particleMesh.frustumCulled=false; this.particleMesh.castShadow=false;`
- Initialize matrices scale 0.
- `this.particlePool = Array.from({length:100},()=>({life:0,...}))`
- `this.particleCursor=0`.
- Add to scene.

Held:
```
this.heldGroup = new Group();
this.heldGroup.visible=false;
this.camera.add(this.heldGroup);
this.heldMaterial = new MeshBasicMaterial({...});
```
- Add after camera in scene. Good.

Highlight:
```
this.highlight = new LineSegments(new EdgesGeometry(new BoxGeometry(1.002,1.002,1.002)), new LineBasicMaterial({color:0x0b1a0e, transparent:true, opacity:0.55, depthTest:true}));
this.highlight.visible=false; this.highlight.renderOrder=5;
scene.add(this.highlight);
```
- Edges lines might be hidden by block surfaces due to z-fighting; scale 1.01. Use 1.008. Fine.

Events:
- `window.addEventListener('resize', ...)`
- document pointerlockchange.
- canvas mousedown/pointerdown, document mousemove/mouseup, wheel, contextmenu.
- window keydown/keyup.
- document visibilitychange: if hidden, save.
- window beforeunload: save.
- `this.canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', ...)`.
- `document.addEventListener('pointerdown', ...)` for touch look? Use canvas.
- Prevent double tap zoom: CSS touch-action none.

Let's think about pointer lock and touch. `this.isTouch` computed. On desktop, canvas mousedown. On touch, pointerdown with pointerType 'touch'. If `pointerType === 'mouse'`, let mousedown handler handle. If touch, look.

`canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { if (e.pointerType === 'mouse') return; if (state!=='playing') return; ... })`.
- But in mobile emulation via Playwright, `pointerType` for touch events would be 'touch'. The capture uses click (mouse) even at mobile viewport, so look not needed. Touch controls visible by width. Fine.
- For actual touch, canvas pointer events work.

`document.addEventListener('mousemove', ...)`: if pointerLocked and state playing -> player.look(movementX, movementY). Else if dragging -> player.look(dx,dy) and track moved. Use e.clientX.
- `mousedown` on canvas: if state playing and !isTouch. If pointerLocked -> actions. Else set dragging and request lock? If we request pointer lock, the subsequent mousemove events become locked and movementX works; dragging flag unnecessary. But requestPointerLock may fail or be async. Set dragging true and last positions.
  - For Playwright capture, click Play triggers pointer lock request. If it succeeds, screenshot fine. If not, dragging fallback. For the screenshot after Play, no mousedown on canvas, so fine.
  - If user clicks canvas while not locked, request lock and set dragging. If lock succeeds, pointerlockchange sets locked; dragging can be set false in handler. If not, drag look.
  - On mouseup: if dragging and moved < 5 and button 0, mine. If lock succeeded, no mouseup? It will fire. Then it might mine unintentionally after locking. Avoid: set `this.suppressClick = true` when requesting lock; on mouseup if suppressClick, reset and skip action.
- When pointerLocked, mousedown on canvas fires button 0 -> mine. Good.
- Right-click when not locked: request? no, set dragging and on mouseup place. But context menu prevented. Good.

`wheel`: if state playing, change slot; prevent default. Add to canvas or window? Use window with `{passive:false}`. If state playing, preventDefault. But scrolling in settings panel should work. Only when state playing. Good.

Keyboard:
- Keydown listener: if target is input/textarea/select, allow Escape only.
- If state playing:
  - Digit1-9 -> selectSlot.
  - KeyE -> openInventory.
  - KeyF -> toggleFly.
  - KeyC or ControlLeft -> down.
  - Space -> preventDefault.
  - Shift -> toggle sprint if setting toggle.
  - Escape -> pause.
- If state paused and Escape -> resume.
- If state inventory and Escape -> closeInventory.
- If state settings and Escape -> closeSettings.
- If state help -> closeHelp.
- If state newworld -> closeNewWorld.
- If state menu and Escape -> nothing.
- Prevent browser shortcuts? no.

`updateInput()`:
- Build input each frame:
```
const s=this.settings.data.controls;
const sprint = s.sprint==='toggle' ? this.sprintToggle : keys.has('ShiftLeft')||keys.has('ShiftRight')||this.touch.sprint;
return {forward:keys.has('KeyW')||keys.has('ArrowUp'), ... , axisX: touch.axisX, axisY: touch.axisY, jump: keys.has('Space')||touch.jump, down: keys.has('ControlLeft')||keys.has('KeyC'), sprint};
```
- If `this.isTouch` and joystick axis > .9 sets touch.sprint. Good.
- In flying, jump ascend.

`loop(now)`:
```
requestAnimationFrame(this.loop);
const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now-this.lastTime)/1000 || 0);
this.lastTime=now;
this.time += dt;
if (this.state==='playing' && this.player) {
  this.player.update(dt, this.updateInput());
  this.player.updateCamera(this.camera);
  this.world.update(dt);
  this.updateHeld(dt);
  this.updateParticles(dt);
  this.updateTarget();
  this.updateTime(dt);
  this.updateSky(dt);
  this.updateClouds(dt);
  this.updateHUD(dt);
  this.autosave(dt);
  this.audio.update(dt, {isNight:this.isNight, underwater:this.player.headUnderwater});
} else if (this.state==='menu') {
  this.updateTime(dt*0.35);
  this.updateSky(dt);
  this.updateClouds(dt);
  this.updateMenuCamera(dt);
  this.world?.update(dt);
  this.audio.update(dt, {isNight:this.isNight, underwater:false});
  this.updateHUD(dt); // fps maybe hidden
} else if (this.state==='inventory' || this.state==='paused') {
  this.updateTime(0); // freeze
  this.updateSky(0);
  this.updateClouds(dt*0.5); // maybe
  this.world?.update(dt*0.5);
  this.player?.updateCamera(this.camera); // keep
  this.updateHeld(dt);
  this.updateParticles(dt);
  this.updateTarget(); // paused? maybe hide
  this.audio.update(dt, ...);
} else if (this.state==='loading') { ... }
if (this.world) this.render();
```
- For paused, we shouldn't call updateTarget (hide highlight). Instead hide. For inventory, hide highlight.
- `updateSky(0)` still needs to update uniforms; yes.
- Menu camera update before sky (focus center).
- `updateTime(dt)` only in playing/menu.
- `updateSky(dt)` uses state to decide focus/camera positions.
- `updateHUD` every frame? It has internal timer. Fine.
- `render` after all.

- The loop starts after init. `this.lastTime=performance.now()`.

- When state loading, skip render (world null or being disposed). Maybe render sky? Loading screen covers. Fine.
- If state paused and world exists, render to show blurred background behind scrim. Good.
- If state settings from menu, world exists and menu camera remains? We should keep camera at menu orbit? When settings opened from menu, the camera stays where it was (menu orbit) but state settings -> loop branch paused -> updateCamera(player) would snap to player! Bad. Need to handle overlays from menu: keep menu camera. Add state 'settings' branch: if overlayReturn==='menu' and state==='settings'/'help'/'newworld', update menu camera. Or track `this.backgroundMode = 'menu'|'game'`. Simpler: in loop, for overlay states, if `this.overlayReturn === 'menu'` use menu camera, else player camera. But overlayReturn may be 'pause'. Good.
- For settings from pause, camera stays player. 
- For new world from pause, background player. Fine.
- For help from menu, menu camera.

- `updateMenuCamera(dt)` also used for overlays from menu. Increment angle only if state menu? Could animate behind settings; nice. Use dt.
- For state settings with overlayReturn menu, call updateMenuCamera(dt).
- For state paused, player camera.

- `updateHeld` only if state playing or paused? In pause, held hidden maybe. Let's hide held in pause/settings. Set `heldGroup.visible = state==='playing'`. For inventory, hide? Inventory overlay covers. Hide. In paused, hide. Simpler: visible only playing. That avoids weird. Good. So in loop updateHeld only playing.
- In menu, hidden.

- `updateSky` must set focus based on background mode: menu camera center vs player.

- `updateTime` while menu: yes. While settings from menu? maybe freeze? The menu time could continue; fine. Use `backgroundMode==='menu'` to advance slowly. But settings from menu is state settings; we can still advance slowly. Let's define `this.isMenuBackdrop = state==='menu' || ((settings/help/newworld) && overlayReturn==='menu')`. In loop, if isMenuBackdrop, updateTime(dt*0.35) and updateMenuCamera(dt). Good.
- For inventory/paused, freeze time.
- For playing, advance.

- Render: `this.renderScene()`.

- `updateHUD` only if state playing/inventory. In menu hidden. For inventory, update clock/fps maybe. Fine.
- In paused, HUD hidden.

- `audio.update` always except loading.

- `autosave` only playing.

`updateTime(dt)`:
```
if (!settings.dayCycle) return;
this.worldTime += dt/(dayLength*60);
if (this.worldTime >= 1) { this.worldTime -= 1; this.day++; }
```
- Initial worldTime 0.34.

`updateSky(dt)`:
- Compute t = worldTime % 1.
- `this.isNight = elevation < -0.05`.
- Set sky uniforms, fog, lights, sun/moon, stars.
- Focus:
```
if (this.isMenuBackdrop()) focus.set(size/2, 20, size/2);
else if (player) focus.copy(player.position).add(0,1,0);
```
- sunLight target.
- `this.sunLight.position.copy(focus).addScaledVector(lightDir, 90); this.sunTarget.position.copy(focus);`
- `this.sunTarget.updateMatrixWorld()` maybe.
- For menu, shadows not needed? Could keep.
- `this.sunMesh.position.copy(camera.position).addScaledVector(sunDir, 260);`
- `this.moonMesh.position.copy(camera.position).addScaledVector(sunDir, -260);`
- `this.stars.position.copy(camera.position); this.stars.rotation.y = this.worldTime * Math.PI * 2;`
- `this.sky.position.copy(camera.position);`
- Fog.
- `this.scene.fog.near = underwater ? 0.1 : 32; far = underwater ? 22 : 160;`
- `this.scene.fog.color.copy(horizon)`; if underwater, set #0a3a55.
- Sun visibility: `sunMesh.visible = elevation > -0.18`; moon `elevation < 0.18`. Sun opacity? MeshBasicMaterial no opacity unless transparent; set transparent true and opacity = smoothstep(-0.18,0.02,elevation)? Sun below horizon should disappear. Use visible.
- Sun mesh scale maybe 18; moon 12.
- Sun material color set from palette sunColor * 2.5. Color components can exceed 1 with `.multiplyScalar(3)`. Set once each frame? Use `this.sunMat.color.copy(sunColor).multiplyScalar(3)`. But `sunColor` is a Color; multiply. Need preallocated.
- Moon color `#dfe9ff` * 1.4.

- Stars material opacity = clamp((-elevation - 0.02) * 3, 0, 1). visible = settings.stars && opacity > 0.01. If stars hidden, no.
- Clouds material color: `cloudColor.copy(nightCloud).lerp(dayCloud, day)`; also tint sunset? Maybe `cloudColor.lerp(sunsetCloud, twilight*0.5)`. Use warm clouds at sunset.
- Cloud opacity 0.94.
- Hemi:
```
this.hemi.color.copy(horizon).lerp(white,0.25);
this.hemi.groundColor.copy(nightGround).lerp(dayGround, day);
this.hemi.intensity = 0.16 + day*0.6;
this.ambient.intensity = 0.05 + day*0.12;
```
- Sun light color:
```
this.lightColor.copy(nightLight).lerp(dayLight, day).lerp(sunsetLight, twilight*0.65);
this.sunLight.color.copy(this.lightColor);
this.sunLight.intensity = 0.18 + day*2.25 + twilight*0.35;
```
At night day=0 twilight=0 => .18. Maybe moonlight .3. Set base 0.26. At sunset day .5? twilight 1 => intensity .26+1.125+.35=1.7 warm. Good.
- `this.sunLight.position` uses `lightDir = elevation > 0.02 ? sunDir : sunDir.clone().negate()`? At sunset elevation 0, use moon? Better use sunDir while elevation >= -0.05, then moon. If elevation < -0.05, light from moon. Use `this.lightDir.copy(sunDir); if (sunDir.y < -0.02) this.lightDir.negate();`
- Shadows from moon at night, cool.
- `this.sunLight.shadow.needsUpdate = true`? Auto.

- Fog color for menu maybe slightly lighter.
- Sky top/horizon colors as above.
- Sky shader uniform sunDir and sunColor; add glow. `uSunDir` should be sunDir even below horizon; glow hidden below. Fine.
- `uSunColor` set to sunColor * 1.2.
